# Costica, the worst highwayman in Barovia (NPC plan batch 2; docs/plans/npc_depth_and_quests.md): Bildrath's cousin, who
# robs politely and never keeps a thing. By day on the Old Svalich Road at the crossroads. Every spoken line was drafted
# by Gemini 4 Argon (Medium) through the ai-bridge and edited by Claude (docs/plans/gemini_batch2/). Nodes, checks, flags
# and exits are Claude's. No quest, no main flag; every node ends in a menu or END; nothing here needs a roll.

~ start
if flag.costica_met
Costica [sad]: Forgive me, I did not recognise your boots through the mist until I had already stepped out of the bushes.
Costica [neutral]: In my trade, once one has emerged from the brambles, etiquette demands the robbery be seen through.
else
set costica_met
Narrator: A thin man steps out of the roadside brambles, holding a notched and rusted blade upright in front of him like a church candle.
Costica [neutral]: Good day, travellers, and my apologies for the interruption.
Costica [afraid]: As a professional highwayman, I must ask you to stand and deliver whatever small coin you can comfortably spare.
Costica [smile]: Do take your time with the clasps on your purses. The damp makes the leather terribly stiff.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Hold on. He has a receipt and an opening figure, so we can talk him down to three dried apricots and a button.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Look at that stance, that grip. It takes real dedication to do every part of a stick-up wrong at once.
interject name:ratatoille: Before you refuse him, I should like to know whether that rye was baked with caraway.
interject tag:blunt: Get out of the road before you drop that thing on your own foot.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if gold >= 2] Hand over two gold. -> pay
* [Intimidation DC 12] Put that down before you hurt yourself. -> scare_ok | scare_fail
* [Insight DC 11] There's something wrong with the way he's holding that sword. -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* Who are you? -> who
* [if flag.costica_paid] What did you do with our gold? -> secret
* [if quest.radus_unsellable_horse == offered] We hear you want a horse. -> svalich_road/radus_horse:costica_horse
* [if quest.radus_unsellable_horse == buyer_found and (flag.tser_pool_brawl_won or flag.vistani_turned_hostile)] Radu's camp has turned on us, so there is no one left to pay his fifteen gold. -> svalich_road/radus_horse:camp_unpaid
* We'll just walk past. -> walk_past
* Goodbye. -> goodbye

~ pay
set costica_paid
gold -2
Costica [smile]: Two whole gold pieces? You are most generous, and a credit to the victims of this valley.
Narrator: He lays his sword in the mud, takes a stub of charcoal and a damp scrap of parchment from his coat, and writes with great concentration.
Costica [neutral]: Your receipt, duly signed, so that no other footpad on the Old Svalich Road may tax you twice in one afternoon.
-> menu

~ scare_ok
Costica [afraid]: Say no more, I beg you. I can see I have misjudged the occasion entirely.
Costica [sad]: It was never my intention to distress travellers of such fierce and admirable bearing.
Costica [neutral]: Please accept my apologies, and this parcel of salted turnip and rye bread by way of amends.
give ration
Costica [smile]: It is quite fresh, I assure you. I shall now step back into the wet bushes.
-> END

~ scare_fail
Costica [angry]: There is no call for that tone, least of all toward a man conducting an honest hold-up.
Costica [sad]: You have no idea how damp it is behind those gorse bushes, waiting six hours for a single cart.
Costica [neutral]: In my trade we strive for a certain roadside civility, even when our customers are rude.
time +15
Narrator: By the time he has finished explaining the difficulties of the profession, a quarter of an hour has gone.
Costica [sad]: Go on, then, and keep your purses. I have quite lost the spirit for brigandage today.
-> END

~ insight_ok
Narrator: His knuckles are white on the hilt, yet he angles the blade away from you, as if terrified it might scratch someone.
Costica [sad]: It was my late grandmother's. She was always most particular about keeping the edge away from company.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: His stiff shoulders are impossible to read in the gloom: a cunning secret, or a cramp from crouching in the ditch.
-> menu

~ who
Costica [neutral]: I am Costica, highwayman of the Old Svalich Road, at your service.
Costica [sad]: Times are lean in my profession. Very few people travel for pleasure, and fewer still carry spare coin.
Costica [neutral]: My cousin Bildrath keeps the mercantile in the village. He says a man must find a trade and stick to it.
Costica [smile]: Everything I plunder I spend at his counter. Family pays ten times the going price, same as everyone, and Bildrath considers that a kindness.
-> menu

~ secret
Costica [smile]: You will be glad to hear your two gold pieces were put to immediate and practical use.
Costica [neutral]: Last month I sold my best hat to my cousin, to cover the rent. He keeps it in his window at ten times the price.
Costica [sad]: Your gold bought me one afternoon of wearing it, which Bildrath rents out by the hour. I do not complain.
Costica [smile]: Do not mistake me for bitter. It is a very good hat, and it was well worth the afternoon.
-> menu

~ walk_past
Narrator: You walk past him along the muddy rut. He turns on his heel to keep facing you, sword still upright, as if nobody has told it the robbery is over.
Costica [afraid]: Pardon me, if it is not too bold, did you not hear the part where I bade you stand and deliver?
Costica [sad]: Tell me honestly, as travellers of the world: should I have pitched my voice lower when I stepped out of the gorse?
-> END

~ goodbye
Costica [neutral]: Safe travels, then, and do mind the deep puddle just past the bend.
Costica [sly]: Beware the shadows of the road, for next time I may well ask for three gold pieces, if it is not an inconvenience.
-> END
